# Allen Relation: BEFORE / MEETS
#
# BEFORE: interval A ends strictly before interval B begins.
#   A before B  iff  A.end < B.start
#
# MEETS: interval A ends at the exact moment interval B begins.
#   A meets B  iff  A.end = B.start
#
# Legal patterns that trigger BEFORE or MEETS:
#   "as from X until the entry into force of Y"
#   "prior to the commencement of"
#   "before the effective date of"
#   "until X enters into force" followed by "upon entry into force"
#   "from X to Y" where Y is a trigger event for a new period
#
# Grounded example (en_contracts_seed0, Article 2.4 + Article 11.1):
#   Pre-entry import period [1.1.2005, entry_into_force) is BEFORE
#   agreement active period [entry_into_force, 31.12.2006].
#   The two periods MEET when the agreement enters into force.

```catala
declaration scope AllenBefore:
  input interval_a_start content date   # start of the earlier period
  input interval_a_end content date     # end of the earlier period
  input interval_b_start content date   # start of the later period
  input interval_b_end content date     # end of the later period
  output is_before content boolean      # A ends strictly before B starts
  output is_meets content boolean       # A ends exactly when B starts
```

## BEFORE

Interval A ends strictly before interval B begins — there is a gap
between the two periods.

```catala
scope AllenBefore:
  date round down
  definition is_before equals
    interval_a_end < interval_b_start
```

## MEETS

Interval A ends at the exact moment interval B begins — no gap,
no overlap. Common in legal transitions where one regime immediately
succeeds another.

```catala
scope AllenBefore:
  definition is_meets equals
    interval_a_end = interval_b_start
```
